# Clean Installation Configuration
# This file documents the clean installation behavior of BST

## Data Persistence Strategy

### What gets deleted on uninstall:
- Database (SQLite): Stored in %APPDATA%/BST/app.db
- localStorage: Stored in %APPDATA%/BST/Local Storage
- Session tokens: Cleared on logout or expiration (30 days)

### What is NOT included in the installer:
- backend/data/ folder (excluded via electron-builder filter)
- Excel file with student data
- Any existing database files

### What needs to be set up after installation:
1. Login with Google account
2. Create database (automatic on first student registration or manual via POST /api/health)
3. Upload Excel file with student data (POST /api/health/upload-excel)

## Technical Implementation

### Database Location (backend/lib/db.js):
- Development: backend/data/dev.db
- Production (Electron): %APPDATA%/BST/app.db (via USER_DATA_PATH env var)
- Fallback: backend/data/app.db

### localStorage Cleanup (frontend/src/contexts/AuthContext.tsx):
- On token expiration: localStorage.clear()
- On logout: localStorage.clear()
- On parse error: localStorage.clear()

### Electron Packaging (launcher/package.json):
- Excludes: backend/data/** (no database, no Excel file)
- User data stored in: app.getPath('userData')

## Endpoints for Initial Setup

### Database:
- GET /api/health - Check database status
- POST /api/health - Create/initialize database

### Excel File:
- POST /api/health/upload-excel - Upload student data Excel file
- GET /api/health/check-excel - Verify Excel file exists and is valid
- POST /api/students/load-excel - Load Excel data into memory

## Environment Variables

### Passed from Electron to Backend:
- USER_DATA_PATH: Path to Electron's userData directory
- NODE_ENV: 'development' or 'production'

## Security Notes

- Tokens expire after 30 days
- No sensitive data persists after uninstall
- Excel file must be uploaded manually (not included in installer)
- Database is created on-demand, not pre-populated
